        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. SSH into any Linux machine (or open WSL2) and navigate to your home directory. Create a project folder, create three empty files inside it with `touch`, then list them with `ls -la`.\n2. Install `htop` with apt, run it, and identify which process is using the most memory.\n3. Start a tmux session, run `sleep 300` inside it, detach, list sessions, and reattach.\n4. Use `df -h` to check available disk space, then use `du -sh ~/.cache/*` to find what's taking up space in your cache.\n5. Transfer a file from your local machine to a remote one using `scp`, then do the same transfer with `rsync` and compare the experience."
      ]
    }
